  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given a string SSS of length NNN consisting of lowercase english alphabets.\n\nIn one operation, you can:\n\n\nChoose any three **consecutive** characters in SSS;\nApply a **circular left shift** operation on the chosen characters.\nFor example, let the string be `codechef`. In one operation, you can:\n\n\nChoose characters S2,S3,S_2, S_3,S2​,S3​, and S4S_4S4​;\nApply a circular left shift to convert S2S3S4S_2S_3S_4S2​S3​S4​ to S3S4S2S_3S_4S_2S3​S4​S2​. Thus, the string becomes `cdeochef`.\nYour task is to find out the number of **distinct** strings that are possible if you apply the above mentioned operation **exactly once**.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN, denoting the length of the string SSS.\nThe second line of each test case contains the string SSS.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line, the number of **distinct** strings that are possible if you apply the above mentioned operation **exactly once** on string SSS.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\leq T \\leq 10^41≤T≤104",
      "3≤N≤1053 \\leq N \\leq 10^53≤N≤105",
      "SSS consists of lowercase english alphabets only.",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 10510^5105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\n5\naabaa\n8\ncodechef",
        "output": "2\n6",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: After applying exactly one operation, the string can become abaaa, abaaa, or aaaab. Hence, two distinct strings are possible.\nTest case 222: Applying operation anywhere in the string leads to a distinct string."
      }
    ]
  },
